;; Area map of the Goose conformance harness (scripts/conformance.bb,
;; docs/javascript-coverage.md decision 7). Every inventoried case is either
;; in :cases with one of the 14 areas or in :excluded with its reason; the
;; runner fails on an unmapped or stale entry.
;;
;; Areas follow the QuickJS audits bbp-34 to bbp-47 (Pellets project bbp,
;; ~/src/big-boy-pants-js) and the area planners light-cljs-762 to -775; the
;; QuickJS case lists below are those audits' "Cases to classify".
;;
;; Origins (labels): :pants-authored (the Pants engine's own synthetic
;; fixtures); :quickjs-selected-text (Pants fixtures whose header says the
;; selected QuickJS lines are byte-for-byte unchanged, only a header, calls or
;; a minimal harness helper added); :quickjs-adapted (Pants fixtures whose
;; header records changed upstream lines or replaced host bindings);
;; :quickjs-per-function (set by the runner: unmodified upstream text,
;; per-function entry); :quickjs-unmodified (a whole upstream file);
;; :bbp-authored (set by the runner for conformance/cases/).
;;
;; Modes: QuickJS-derived cases run as sloppy scripts, as qjs runs them (a
;; "use strict" directive in the text still applies); bbp- and
;; Pants-authored cases run as strict scripts, as the Pants command line and
;; the Goose exporter do by default; :module cases run as modules.
;;
;; :pants-gap REASON: a case of a feature the Pants engine does not implement
;; (its VM is not extended for Goose); it is scored against QuickJS alone.
{:areas
 {:lexing-parsing "Lexing, literals, parsing and source positions (bbp-34, light-cljs-775)"
  :operators-values "Expression operators, primitive values and coercions (bbp-35, light-cljs-762)"
  :statements-loops "Statements, loops, labels and completion values (bbp-36, light-cljs-763)"
  :functions-scope "Functions, scope, closures, arguments and eval (bbp-37, light-cljs-764)"
  :objects-classes "Objects, properties, prototypes, classes and symbols (bbp-38, light-cljs-766)"
  :core-builtins "Array, String, Number, Math and JSON built-ins (bbp-39, light-cljs-767)"
  :collections-weak "Map/Set, typed arrays, weak references and finalization (bbp-40, light-cljs-769)"
  :date-regexp "Date and RegExp built-ins (bbp-41, light-cljs-770)"
  :bigint "BigInt (bbp-42, light-cljs-771)"
  :intl "Intl (ECMA-402) locale built-ins (bbp-43, light-cljs-774)"
  :exceptions "Exceptions and try/catch/finally control flow (bbp-44, light-cljs-765)"
  :using "Explicit resource management, using / await using (bbp-45, light-cljs-772)"
  :generators-async "Generators, async functions and promise jobs (bbp-46, light-cljs-768)"
  :modules "ES modules (bbp-47, light-cljs-773)"}

 ;; Per-function entries come from each file's own calls. bbp-36 also lists
 ;; test_loop.js's test_cyclic_labels, which upstream defines but never calls:
